<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<%- include('../partials/breadcrumbs') %>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Returns policy</h1>
    <p>What can be returned, and the route a return has to take.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>The window</h2>
    <p>
      The shop's stated return window is <%= returnsWindowDays %> days from the day the item is transferred
      to you. Tell the shop inside that window if you intend to return something.
    </p>

    <h2>Firearms</h2>
    <p>
      A firearm that has already been transferred to you cannot be dropped in the mail. Under federal law a
      non licensee may not ship a handgun by the United States Postal Service at all, and a common carrier
      shipment has to be declared to the carrier. In practice a firearm return runs back through a Federal
      Firearms Licensee: you contact the shop first, the shop agrees the route in writing, and the firearm
      moves licensee to licensee.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once <%= jurisdiction.transactionRecordForm %> has been completed and the firearm has left the counter
      it is a used firearm, so a return is assessed on condition and is not automatic. Contact the shop
      before you do anything else and follow the instructions you are given.
    </p>

    <h2>Parts and accessories</h2>
    <p>
      Unused parts in their original packaging can normally be returned inside the window. Parts that have
      been fitted, modified or refinished cannot, because they can no longer be sold as new and their
      condition cannot be verified.
    </p>

    <h2>Faulty items</h2>
    <p>
      A manufacturing fault is handled under the manufacturer warranty and under the implied warranty
      provisions of the Texas Business and Commerce Code, whichever gives you more. Tell the shop what happened, and do not attempt a repair first, because that
      normally voids the warranty.
    </p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>
      An accepted return is refunded by the method used to pay. A transfer fee already paid to a third party
      licensee is not refundable by this shop, because that money went to another business. Sales tax is
      refunded with the item price where the sale is reversed.
    </p>

    <h2>How to start a return</h2>
    <p>
      Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> with your order reference and a description of the problem.
      Do not send identity documents or licence numbers through the form.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
